# Database Clients Guide

LLAE provides asynchronous database clients for Redis and PostgreSQL.

## Redis Client
Main module: [scripts/db/redis.lua](mdc:scripts/db/redis.lua)
- Supports all Redis commands
- Pub/Sub functionality
- Pipeline operations
- Automatic type conversion

Example usage: [examples/redis.lua](mdc:examples/redis.lua)
Documentation: [docs/db/redis.md](mdc:docs/db/redis.md)

## PostgreSQL Client
Main module: [scripts/db/pgsql.lua](mdc:scripts/db/pgsql.lua)
- Asynchronous queries
- Multiple authentication methods
- Binary data handling
- Type conversion

Example usage: [examples/pgsql.lua](mdc:examples/pgsql.lua)
Documentation: [docs/db/pgsql.md](mdc:docs/db/pgsql.md)

## Common Features
Both clients:
- Use coroutines for async operations
- Handle automatic reconnection
- Support connection pooling
- Provide type-safe data handling
